# The bundled engine is checked file by file against SHA-256 digests (release/baseline/), so git must
# never rewrite its line endings (Git for Windows does by default with core.autocrlf=true).
engine/** -text
# Its hash decides whether an unedited studio-profile SOUL may be upgraded.
profile/SOUL.md -text
# The desktop half and the player frame shim are built from desktop-src/ by tools/bundle.mjs, and each
# banner carries a hash of both: their bytes must be the same on every checkout. A merge must never write conflict
# markers into the bundle (a linked checkout hot-loads it): with -merge git keeps our side and reports
# the conflict. Merge the sources, then rebuild.
desktop-src/**/*.js text eol=lf
desktop-src/**/*.png binary
tools/bundle.mjs text eol=lf
desktop/plugin.js text eol=lf -merge linguist-generated=true
player/frame-shim.js text eol=lf -merge linguist-generated=true
